{#
/**
 * @file
 * testimonials — the quotes carousel (components/testimonials.css,
 * js/testimonials.js): the team panel's bar reused — arrows leading, the
 * counter over the quote column, THE hairline under — and the quotes in the
 * slot, one showing at a time. The script counts the quotes (not the
 * children: an empty slot holds a placeholder in the editor), writes the
 * counter and steps; data-count="1" takes the bar away (user ask, Sep 2026:
 * "an option to have a single testimonial (hide the left right arrows and
 * the 01 / 06 and line for single)").
 *
 * THE BOX, ALWAYS, IN THE QUOTE'S COLOURS (user call, 23 Oct 2026:
 * "Testimonials define the colours … so why are there two other places to
 * manage colours never seen?" — the group's own Box pick and Custom pair
 * went): the Columns box's own markup and classes around the carousel — a
 * one-column Columns box, so columns.css's padding, corner, grounds and
 * re-declared aliases apply unchanged — on the chameleon's class, the pair
 * as its two custom properties. The pair is the FIRST quote's, read off the
 * rendered slot (each Testimonial item carries its Ground and Ink as
 * data-bg / data-ink), so the page draws in the right colours with no
 * flash; js/testimonials.js then re-dresses the box as the quotes turn. A
 * quote without a pair (the fields are required on the form, but an older
 * record may be blank) falls to light grey on black.
 */
#}
{% set rendered %}{% block quotes %}{{ quotes }}{% endblock %}{% endset %}
{% set hex = '/^#(?:[0-9a-f]{3,4}|[0-9a-f]{6}|[0-9a-f]{8})$/i' %}
{% set first_bg = 'data-bg="' in rendered ? rendered|split('data-bg="', 2)[1]|split('"', 2)[0] : '' %}
{% set first_ink = 'data-ink="' in rendered ? rendered|split('data-ink="', 2)[1]|split('"', 2)[0] : '' %}
{% set pair = first_bg matches hex and first_ink matches hex %}
{% set box_style = '--work-article-bg: ' ~ (pair ? first_bg : 'var(--light-grey)') ~ '; --work-article-text: ' ~ (pair ? first_ink : 'var(--black)') %}
{# The site's scroll-in entrance (data-animate — the fade-up the pull quotes
   and the stats band wear; js/reveal.js, utilities/animations.css) on the
   box. The velocity skew came on 20 Oct 2026 (user ask: "can the load and
   scroll skew animation be applied to this") — js/testimonials.js writes it
   on the box the quote colours paint, which also takes over the fade-up
   when it is an outer Columns box. #}
<div class="columns columns--1 columns--gap-normal columns--box theme-work-article testimonials__box" data-animate style="{{ box_style }}"><div class="columns__col">
<section class="testimonials" data-testimonials{% if label %} aria-roledescription="carousel" aria-label="{{ label }}"{% endif %}>
  <div class="testimonials__bar">
    <div class="testimonials__steps">
      {# one quote: a small quotation mark where the arrows would be (user
         call, 22 Sep 2026); the CSS swaps them on data-count="1" #}
      <span class="testimonials__quotemark" aria-hidden="true">&ldquo;</span>
      <button class="testimonials__arrow" type="button" data-testimonials-prev aria-label="{{ 'Previous quote'|t }}">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 12H4"/><path d="m10 6-6 6 6 6"/></svg>
      </button>
      <button class="testimonials__arrow" type="button" data-testimonials-next aria-label="{{ 'Next quote'|t }}">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12h16"/><path d="m14 6 6 6-6 6"/></svg>
      </button>
    </div>
    <p class="testimonials__counter" aria-live="polite"><span data-testimonials-index>01</span><span class="testimonials__of"> / <span data-testimonials-count>01</span></span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="testimonials__track">
    {{ rendered }}
  </div>
</section>
</div></div>
